WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
One death sentence is set aside in Saudi Arabia, changing a Sri Lankan workers' fate. This is Omni View Africa &amp; Middle East, episode 22. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. The man is a no-gen Sivirasa, 27, a Sri Lankan migrant worker. Columbus Deputy Foreign Minister, Arun Hemachandra, says Saudi Arabia's Supreme Court has lifted the death sentence imposed over a Facebook comment. An appellate court had condemned him in September for blasphemy against Islam and the Prophet Muhammad.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:30.100
Ahmed.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.220
Hemichandra posted on Wednesday that the top court had set that sentence aside, and he

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.780
thanked the authorities and the legal teams of both countries.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.880
Police took Sivirasa in July.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.140
In late June, video of a young Muslim man kicking a dog that was following Hindu pilgrims

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.600
spread online and started a religious argument.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.940
Another user insulted a Hindu deity.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.420
Sivirasa answered in Tamil with an insult to the prophet, deleted it, and put up an apology.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.720
A screenshot still reached his employer and Saudi officials.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.840
Before the death sentence, the Al-Asa criminal court had given him five years in a fine

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.160
of three million Saudi reels, about $800,000.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.600
Lawmaker Faser Mustafa, who is in the talks with Riyadh, told BBC Sinhala the death sentence

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.220
is overturned and that they are now reading the Supreme Court's latest ruling.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.240
The BBC says it is not clear whether the case goes on or whether he stays in detention.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.380
His family had said they last had direct contact on the 28th of September.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:31.460
On Tuesday, human rights watch researcher Joey Shea said Saudi authorities should stop

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:36.700
using abusive laws to impose extraordinary sentences for speech, above all against migrant

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.160
workers who have few protections.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:44.225
In Syria's Hama countryside, four security personnel are dead after an ambush on Tuesday

00:01:44.225 --> 00:01:44.585
night.

00:01:44.985 --> 00:01:49.485
The national reports that two patrols were hit on the motorway between Salamia and Atheria.

00:01:50.085 --> 00:01:54.945
Interior Ministry spokesman Nour Al-Baba condemned the attack and said the crime will not stop

00:01:54.945 --> 00:01:59.105
the hunt for those responsible. He said the killings will harden the forces' determination

00:01:59.105 --> 00:02:03.205
to protect civilians. Internal security says the search is still underway.

00:02:03.725 --> 00:02:08.185
The road runs east of Hama City toward the Syrian desert. On a corridor into the east,

00:02:08.505 --> 00:02:11.525
in country where armed groups and ISIS militants have struck before.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:19.190
South Africa has put a record 962,832 candidates into the 2026 metric exams.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:24.570
The Daily Maverick says they began on 13 October and run to 26 November.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:30.830
Basic Education Minister Sivue Guarube told a briefing on the 11th that preparations were done.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:38.730
815,000 and 51 candidates are full-time, and 147,781 are part-time.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:44.730
About 7,100 centers are open, and more than 51,000 educators have been hired to mark.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:49.230
Provinces, she said, will be judged on bachelor passes, distinctions,

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.430
how many learners they keep, and how they do in mathematics,

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:55.010
physics, physical sciences, accounting, and economics.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.170
Umelusi has approved the papers.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.730
Private one-to-one lessons have been reported at up to 750

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:04.190
rand-an-hour, so the same report points to free help.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.370
A capsule-line tool called Saving Grace, which Charles

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.390
McKembe says grade 12 learners can use at no charge,

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.810
and see Avula, zero rated on M-T-N and cell C.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:17.950
Andrew Barrett, who runs Oliko Maths Education, says most of

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.410
the learners they see are many years behind in Maths.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:25.770
Oliko has worked in after-school clubs since 2008, and it now tutors in person in the

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.990
Western Cape, Gautang, and Lampopo.

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:33.403
In Caberra, two residents want every rand accounted for on the old wild bridge.

00:03:33.943 --> 00:03:39.803
Francis Jeffrey from Swartcops and Eileen Leander from Allos told the Daily Maverick that 2.4

00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:41.763
million rand of upgrades look like a mess.

00:03:42.283 --> 00:03:43.743
Jeffrey asked where the money went.

00:03:44.163 --> 00:03:48.463
Leander called the job a laughing stock and told the municipality to come and clean it up.

00:03:48.463 --> 00:03:52.703
The bridge crosses the Swartcops River between Amsterdam Hoke and Swartcops.

00:03:52.943 --> 00:03:57.523
It opened in September 1879, one of the oldest in Nelson Mandela Bay.

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:02.943
A bright repaint in 2016 gave it the nickname Smartie Bridge, and that work took off the

00:04:02.943 --> 00:04:03.823
original height bars.

00:04:04.503 --> 00:04:08.963
Trucks then used it as a shortcut to factories and truck stops, despite a five-ton limit.

00:04:09.463 --> 00:04:11.263
Complaints about the damage go back years.

00:04:11.843 --> 00:04:17.123
The city says the 2.4 million rand paid for approaches, roadworks, curbing, calming

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:20.603
measures and signs. The two women say the ground does not show it.

00:04:21.043 --> 00:04:25.183
In February, the same newsroom found trucks had already smashed new plastic height bars

00:04:25.183 --> 00:04:30.323
and vehicles had kept breaking the curbs. On Friday the 9th of October, those plastic

00:04:30.323 --> 00:04:35.223
bars were gone, and several trucks still crossed. Leander says traffic officers sometimes

00:04:35.223 --> 00:04:40.003
watch, then leave after about 15 minutes. She says the deck vibrates under the weight.

00:04:40.443 --> 00:04:42.903
She and Jeffrey Fierre officials will wait for a disaster.

00:04:42.903 --> 00:04:48.163
Director, Democratic Alliance Ward 16 counselor Werner Senegal called the work absolutely

00:04:48.163 --> 00:04:52.163
shoddy and said he cannot see 2.4 million Rand in what was finished.

00:04:52.483 --> 00:04:57.003
His motion for a full account and for upgrade plans was accepted by the Municipal Public

00:04:57.003 --> 00:04:57.743
Accounts Committee.

00:04:58.143 --> 00:04:59.943
A report must trace every Rand.

00:05:00.243 --> 00:05:04.863
He says the detail waits until after the Municipal election on the 4th of November, then

00:05:04.863 --> 00:05:06.023
goes on in the new term.

00:05:06.543 --> 00:05:10.743
Leander says Allows children have to walk that bridge every school day to reach Swartcops.

00:05:11.323 --> 00:05:15.663
Swartcops children do not, and she says Allos children cannot be sent along the railway.

00:05:16.323 --> 00:05:21.563
Gaps in the railings have stood open so long that children walk in the middle of the road and step aside for traffic.

00:05:22.023 --> 00:05:25.223
She was warned off trying to close the gaps with wire and chevron tape.

00:05:25.803 --> 00:05:30.223
A temporary shutdown during the works lasted two weeks, and for those two weeks, she said,

00:05:30.623 --> 00:05:32.103
the children could cross without cars.

