A floor still laid at Elansburg wilderness cottages in Tancua-Kuru National Park.

00:06:26.895 --> 00:06:31.955
Haifa, Israel's third largest city, may lose a sister city tie with Hackney and East London

00:06:31.955 --> 00:06:38.155
that has stood since 1968. Residents there are being asked through today, the 14th of October.

00:06:38.315 --> 00:06:43.715
whether the link should end. Al Jazeera says the Green Party-led council voted on the 28th of July

00:06:43.715 --> 00:06:48.155
to end it in principle, citing the Burrow's values and human rights commitments in the

00:06:48.155 --> 00:06:53.415
setting of Israel's war on Gaza. Counselors decide after that consultation and a review of

00:06:53.415 --> 00:06:58.755
twinning policy. These breaks are often symbolic. Several British councils cut or froze links

00:06:58.755 --> 00:07:05.226
with Russian cities after the 2022 invasion of Ukraine. In Sudan, the question is whether political

00:07:05.226 --> 00:07:10.106
groups should join a dialogue prepared inside Army-held cartoon. More than three years into

00:07:10.106 --> 00:07:14.826
the war between the Sudanese armed forces and the rapid support forces, a self-appointed

00:07:14.826 --> 00:07:20.386
committee of 19 public figures chaired by Offad University President Kazim Badri, launched

00:07:20.386 --> 00:07:25.626
that effort in August. The members had met Army Chief General Abdel Fata Al-Berhan, who

00:07:25.626 --> 00:07:29.946
also heads the Sovereignty Council, and asked for legal limits on opposition politicians

00:07:29.946 --> 00:07:34.466
to be lifted. Authorities then decreed that certain politically motivated charges would

00:07:34.466 --> 00:07:38.966
be dropped for Sudanese abroad, who come home for talks, and that participants would get

00:07:38.966 --> 00:07:40.266
temporary legal protection.

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:45.746
A senior researcher at the Sierra-Michaelsen Institute, writing in Al Jazeera, says the suffering

00:07:45.746 --> 00:07:49.446
is already immense, and a military result alone cannot rebuild the state.

00:07:49.966 --> 00:07:51.446
Previous mediation has failed.

00:07:51.786 --> 00:07:56.206
The researcher says, so ceasefire work and aid access should run alongside preparations

00:07:56.206 --> 00:07:56.766
to talk.

00:07:57.266 --> 00:08:01.526
The committee says it is not negotiating the country's future and not writing the agenda.

00:08:01.526 --> 00:08:05.126
It's stated job is to get Sudanese actors into the same room.

00:08:05.546 --> 00:08:09.246
The researcher says throwing the effort out before it has proved itself would be too

00:08:09.246 --> 00:08:13.766
soon, and that seeing Al-Berhan was necessary because only he could grant those protections,

00:08:14.186 --> 00:08:15.426
not a blessing of his rule.

00:08:16.534 --> 00:08:21.414
Samud, the civilian coalition led by former Prime Minister Abdullah Hamdok and Tassiz,

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:24.914
an alliance that includes the rapid support forces, refuse it.

00:08:25.254 --> 00:08:26.794
They doubt the committee is independent.

00:08:27.214 --> 00:08:31.254
They warn that talks on Army ground could legitimize Al-Berhan and lock in the split.

00:08:31.254 --> 00:08:34.114
The launch was in Cartoum, under Army control.

00:08:34.574 --> 00:08:36.734
The same researcher calls those worries legitimate.

00:08:37.254 --> 00:08:38.514
The 19 were not elected.

00:08:38.894 --> 00:08:43.294
They do not speak for every camp, and if the effort sticks too close to the army, opponents

00:08:43.294 --> 00:08:45.094
will read it as Al-Berhan's project.

00:08:45.514 --> 00:08:49.854
Their absence still matters, the researcher writes, because no single current can carry

00:08:49.854 --> 00:08:53.974
a crisis this deep, and the committee has yet to show it can reach people outside army

00:08:53.974 --> 00:08:57.694
areas, including the displaced, freely and without intimidation.

